{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Moved verbatim out of the description to bring it under the 8,000-character completion admission limit (it was 8,894). Nothing else in these sections changed.\n\n### Why the index is stat-dirty — external, already identified\n\nA concurrent session made a file copy of the tracker worktree at `.rebar/worktrees/fix-df72-stale-snapshot-close/.rebar/scratch/df72-23558/tracker-copy`. Its `.git` file carried the original's absolute `gitdir:` pointer, so the copy and the real `.tickets-tracker` shared one admin dir, one `refs/heads/tickets`, and one `index`. Each tree's git invalidated the other's stat cache. The same handle produced bug `affordable-omphacite-sunfish` (both remotes deleted from the shared `.git/config`). That writer has exited.\n\n**This condition is not exotic.** Any store large enough, or host loaded enough, to push `git merge` past 30 s produces the identical false \"could not auto-merge\". The store is designed to grow, so this fails closed with a wrong diagnosis as a matter of scale, not only after this incident.\n\n## Local repair of this checkout\n\nTracked as its own acceptance criterion below and performed only through supported rebar paths (`rebar fsck-recover`, else `rebar tracker-maintenance`). Never ad-hoc raw git in the tracker, never `git stash`, and never a reset/fast-forward of the shared checkout, which may hold uncommitted operator WIP. **If recovery would require `--force` on any surface, stop and escalate to the user rather than forcing.** Divergence was 4/32 when filed and 12/46 at 22:25 PDT."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793691974492953048,"uuid":"6ee62453-f7fc-4cfb-8119-454a575340fa"}